  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the highest-priority need is to establish a reliable performance baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest and cheapest configuration in the search space: it uses the most basic RNA encoder (PCA), a single profile (no aggregation needed), and no image modality. This gives a fast, low-variance reference point. All subsequent experiments—testing multiprofile aggregation, learned encoders (scVI, scGPT), image modality, and multimodal fusion—can be interpreted relative to this floor. Starting here maximizes information per experiment: if it performs well, we know the task is tractable with minimal machinery; if it underperforms, we immediately learn which axis (encoder quality, multi-profile aggregation, or image modality) to explore next. Under a limited budget, spending the first slot on the cheapest, most interpretable baseline is the most efficient use of resources."
}

